# Frontend build-time environment.
#
# Loaded by Vite from apps/web/.env at build & dev time.
#
# !!! READ THIS BEFORE ADDING ANYTHING !!!
# Anything prefixed with `VITE_` is INLINED INTO THE PUBLIC BUNDLE during
# build and is visible to anyone who loads the app. Never put secrets here.
# Backend keys (Mongo URI, Anthropic API key, OAuth client secrets, session
# signing keys) belong exclusively in apps/api/.env.
#
# Variables WITHOUT the `VITE_` prefix are not exposed to client code, but
# this file is still public-by-convention — keep secrets out of it entirely.
#
# In production, your hosting platform (Vercel/Netlify/Cloudflare Pages)
# provides these at build time via its environment-variable settings.

# Where the API lives.
# - Dev: leave as `/api`. The Vite dev server proxies `/api` → http://localhost:3001
#   so the browser never makes cross-origin calls.
# - Prod: either keep `/api` (if web and api share the same origin behind a
#   reverse proxy / CDN) or set to the absolute API URL
#   (e.g. https://api.musy.example.com).
VITE_API_URL=/api
